-> ExecutorService: It can create a ThreadPool
        Threads -> creating - using - terminating

        OS Threads (native threads) -> JVM uses OS Threads (Platform threads) ->

        - ThreadPool - pool of Threads. (It is like, if we have 100 tasks and 10 threads pool, then those 100 tasks are done by 10 threads by reusing these 10 threads)

        - Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10); - This brings 10 Threads from OS and runs those 10 Threads. and after done with task we need to shutdown()
        - Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor(); - brings single thread.

